I've compiled Nethack using Cygwin under Windows XP.  I don't think you
can use DJGCC under XP.  At least you couldn't with the last version I
tried.

If make doesn't run you probably didn't install all of the features of
cygwin you need.  You aren't going to be able to compile it without
make.  You can't use gcc against a make file, since gcc is a C compiler
and needs C source file as its input.

You might try
http://planetexpress.homedns.org/nethack/compile_cygwin.txt

